  "_about": "INDB fried recipes appear to count all the frying oil as eaten (e.g. Poori 738 kcal/100 g, 78 g fat). For each code below the build removes the unabsorbed oil so fat per 100 g of food equals the target, then re-expresses every nutrient per 100 g of the remaining food. Piece and serving weights shrink by the same amount. Removed oil E (g per 100 g INDB) = (F - T) / (1 - T/100). Result is labelled source 'estimate', with the original INDB values kept for reference. Targets are typical fat levels for that kind of dish; edit and re-run tools/build_foods.py to change them. Only applied when INDB fat is more than 3 g above the target.",
